TITLE:: MultiLevelLibraryBrowser
summary::  A multiLevel browser for libraries
categories:: GUI>Views, Libraries>jostMlib
related:: jostMLib, Classes/Library, Classes/Archive

DESCRIPTION::
A  window with a multiLevel browser for libraries

If the wslib  Quark is installed, you can delete an item with warning using the delete key.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Create a MultiLevelLibraryBrowser

ARGUMENT:: title
The window title of the view

ARGUMENT:: action
an action to be performed on the value of a bottom level item.
code::
{|browser,currentPath, item| [browser,currentPath, item].postln}; // example
::

ARGUMENT:: source
A Dictionary, Library, or Archive

returns:: a MultiLevelLibraryBrowser


METHOD:: defaultPrefix
a global directory prefix

default: nil
METHOD:: defaultSuffix
a global directory suffix

default: nil

INSTANCEMETHODS::
PRIVATE::init

METHOD:: load
ARGUMENT:: source
An  Archive, Library,  or MultiLevelIdentityDictionary,
ARGUMENT:: startpath
further arguments separated by commas.

example:  \idePrefs,\Documentation


METHOD:: fontSize


METHOD:: dirPrefix
an ascii prefix to dir names, default ""

METHOD:: dirSuffix
an ascii suffix to dir names, default " -> ".

METHOD:: currentPath

METHOD:: autowidth
boolean true

PRIVATE:: attributes

METHOD:: listViews


PRIVATE:: prGetItems

PRIVATE:: prClearBelow

PRIVATE:: startPath


PRIVATE:: prCurrentPath

METHOD:: action
METHOD:: selectedIndices
METHOD:: colWidth

PRIVATE:: prAddLevel


PRIVATE:: prItemBuildAction

PRIVATE:: dict

METHOD:: reload

PRIVATE:: prCleanKey

PRIVATE:: prSetAttributes

METHOD:: view

PRIVATE:: itemBuildFunction



EXAMPLES::

code::
MultiLevelLibraryBrowser("Archive",{|b,k,v|
    "--".postln;
    k.join(" -> ").post;": ".post;v.postln;
    b.selectedIndices.postln;
},Archive.global);

// if the wslib quark is installed, you can delete items using the delete key.

// or load a subpath
// (Just an example, that path must actually exist)
MultiLevelLibraryBrowser("Archive",{|b,k,v|
    "--".postln;
    k.join(" -> ").post;": ".post;v.postln;
    b.selectedIndices.postln;}
).load(Archive.global, \idePrefs,\Documentation)

::